    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThe difference of squares formula states the product of the sum and the difference of two monomials is equal to the difference of their squares:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2]\n\nContent:\nWe can check that this result is correct by expanding the binomial in the usual way, as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n({\\color{blue}a} + {\\color{red}b})(a - b) &= \\[5pt]\n{\\color{blue}a}(a - b) + {\\color{red}b}(a - b) &= \\[5pt]\na^2 - ab + ab - b^2 &= \\[5pt]\na^2 - b^2 \\,& {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n}]\n\nContent:\nNotice that the middle two terms [MATH: - ab] and [MATH: ab] cancel each other out, leaving only [MATH: a^2 - b^2.]\n\nContent:\nIf the order of multiplication is switched, the formula still remains the same:\n[MATH: (a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Finding a Product Using the Difference of Squares Formula\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: (x + 3)(x - 3).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe will use the difference of square formula:\n\n[MATH: (a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2]\n\nSubstituting [MATH: a=x] and [MATH: b=3,] we have\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(x + 3)(x - 3) &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 - 3^2 &= \\[5pt]\nx^2 - 9.\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (z + 1)(z \u2212 1) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: z^{2} \u2212 2z \u2212 1]\nb. [MATH: z^{2} \u2212 2z + 1]\nc. [MATH: z^{2} + 2z + 1]\nd. [MATH: z^{2} \u2212 1]\ne. [MATH: z^{2} + 2z \u2212 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nExpand the following product.[MATH: (x + sqrt(6))(x \u2212 sqrt(6)) =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Finding the Product of Two Binomials With Leading Coefficients\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: (5x - 4)(5x + 4) .]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe will use the difference of square formula:\n\n[MATH: (a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2]\n\nSubstituting [MATH: a=5x] and [MATH: b=4,] we have\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(5x - 4)(5x + 4) &= \\[5pt]\n(5x)^2 - (4)^2 &= \\[5pt]\n25x^2 - 16.\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nExpand the following product.[MATH: (4x + 9)(4x \u2212 9) =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (3x + 2y)(3x \u2212 2y) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 9x^{2} \u2212 4y^{2}]\nb. [MATH: 9x^{2} + 12xy + 4y^{2}]\nc. [MATH: 9x^{2} + 4y^{2}]\nd. [MATH: 9x^{2} \u2212 12xy + 4y^{2}]\ne. [MATH: 9x^{2} + 12xy \u2212 4y^{2}]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Finding the Product of Two Nonlinear Binomials\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: (6x + y^2)(6x - y^2) .]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe will use the difference of square formula:\n\n[MATH: (a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2]\n\nSubstituting [MATH: a=6x] and [MATH: b=y^2,] we have\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n(6x + y^2)(6x - y^2) &= \\[5pt]\n(6x)^2 - \\left(y^2\\right)^2 &= \\[5pt]\n36x^2 - y^4.\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (c^{2} + d^{3})(c^{2} \u2212 d^{3}) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: c^{2} \u2212 d^{5}]\nb. [MATH: c^{4} + 2c^{2}d^{3} \u2212 d^{6}]\nc. [MATH: c^{4} \u2212 d^{6}]\nd. [MATH: c^{4} \u2212 2c^{2}d^{3} \u2212 d^{6}]\ne. [MATH: 2c^{2} \u2212 2d^{3}]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (3x^{2} \u2212 2y)(3x^{2} + 2y) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 9x^{4} \u2212 12x^{2}y \u2212 4y^{2}]\nb. [MATH: 9x^{4} + 12x^{2}y \u2212 4y^{2}]\nc. [MATH: 9x^{4} \u2212 4y^{2}]\nd. [MATH: 9x^{4} + 4y^{2}]\ne. [MATH: 9x^{4} + 6x^{2}y \u2212 4y^{2}]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Example: Finding the Product of Two Binomials Containing General Exponents\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpand [MATH: (2x^n-1)(2x^n+1).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe will use the difference of square formula:\n\n[MATH: (a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2]\n\nSubstituting [MATH: a=2x^n] and [MATH: b=1,] we have\n\n[MATH: (2x^{n} \u2212 1)(2x^{n} + 1)|=; (2x^{n})^{2} \u2212 (1)^{2}|=; 2^{2} \u22c5 (x^{n})^{2} \u2212 1|=; 4x^{2n} \u2212 1.]\n\n---\n\nItem 12 \u2014 Question 7\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (x^{n} + 5)(x^{n} \u2212 5) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: x^{n} \u2212 25]\nb. [MATH: x^{2n} \u2212 25]\nc. [MATH: x^{2n} + 25]\nd. [MATH: x^{2n} \u2212 10x^{n} \u2212 25]\ne. [MATH: x^{n} \u2212 5]\n\n---\n\nItem 13 \u2014 Question 8\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (x^{n} + 3y^{n})(x^{n} \u2212 3y^{n}) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: x^{2n} \u2212 9y^{2n}]\nb. [MATH: x^{2n} + 6x^{n}y^{n} \u2212 9y^{2n}]\nc. [MATH: x^{2n} + 9y^{2n}]\nd. [MATH: x^{2n} + 3x^{n}y^{n} \u2212 9y^{2n}]\ne. [MATH: x^{2n} \u2212 6x^{n}y^{n} \u2212 9y^{2n}]"
  }
